    "contentEn": "If you are thinking of getting married in Turin with a civil ceremony, then get ready because the city truly offers many possibilities. Whether you want an intimate and simple ceremony or dream of something more spectacular. Let's start from the beginning: a civil wedding in Turin is celebrated before the Registrar and requires two witnesses. Before setting the date, you must complete the marriage banns, which serve to confirm that there are no legal impediments. Once completed, you must wait at least twelve days and have up to 180 days to get married, so the advice is to act in good time. Obviously, do not forget the identity documents of the spouses and witnesses, otherwise, no ceremony. As for the location, you can go for the classic option by choosing the municipal halls, such as the Sala Matrimoni (Wedding Hall) or the Sala Juvarra. These are elegant but simple spaces, perfect for a more intimate ceremony, and if at least one of the spouses is a resident of Turin, they usually have no costs. The Sala Matrimoni can host about sixty people, while the Juvarra can accommodate up to ninety-nine. However, if you want your ceremony to have a bit more magic, then it is really worth considering the stately venues, those historic locations that give an incredible atmosphere to the entire event. I'm talking about places like Palazzo Madama, the Accademia delle Scienze, the Museo del Risorgimento, the Teatro Carignano, Palazzo Chiablese, and the Sala Marmi of Palazzo Civico. These halls have a unique charm and, yes, they require a greater investment, but the result is absolutely worth it. Bookings are made through the Ufficio Matrimoni Aulici (Stately Weddings Office), by writing to matrimoniaulici@comune.torino.it, and the cost varies from approximately eight hundred euros for the Sala Marmi to two thousand for Palazzo Madama or the Teatro Carignano. tap images to enlarge Paolo We chose Enrico for a pregnancy photoshoot, he immediately made us feel at ease, super helpful and patient even with our little dog. We highly recommend him. We had our photoshoot with Enrico. An exquisite person. Professional, helpful, and very knowledgeable. We highly recommend him to anyone who wants a personalized photographic work. Ermanno we had our photoshoot with Enrico. An exquisite person. Professional, helpful, and very knowledgeable. We highly recommend him to anyone who wants a personalized photographic work. Michela Enrico did our wedding photoshoot, June 2025. Available, professional. During the service, we also had fun, thus creating a friendly atmosphere that allowed us to be spontaneous and spend our day naturally, cheerfully, and having fun. Thank you, Enrico. A little trick I want to share. If you choose a stately venue, keep an eye on the natural light. Some halls become truly spectacular in the late afternoon, and this makes a huge difference for photos. And speaking of photos, this is no laughing matter. A professional photographer by your side is essential. I'm not just talking about beautiful shots, but about someone who knows how to tell the emotions of the day, capture those glances, those hugs, the spontaneous smiles that would otherwise escape. A good photographer knows how to use light, enhance the location, and move without disturbing the ceremony, so every image looks natural yet meticulously curated. And when you look back at the photos in ten or twenty years, you'll thank yourself for having invested in professionalism. A civil wedding in Turin can be simple and intimate or spectacular and scenic, it depends on what you dream of. The important thing is to plan everything in advance, choose the right location, coordinate other details like flowers, makeup, and accessibility for guests, and above all, ensure that every moment is captured by expert hands. In the end, it's the most important day of your life, and every detail, from the choice of the hall to the light in the photos, will contribute to making it truly unforgettable. WATCH A VIDEO WITH THE WEDDING ALBUM OF SOME COUPLES. A little trick I want to share. If you choose a stately venue, keep an eye on the natural light. Some halls become truly spectacular in the late afternoon, and this makes a huge difference for photos. And speaking of photos, this is no laughing matter. A professional photographer by your side is essential. I'm not just talking about beautiful shots, but about someone who knows how to tell the emotions of the day, capture those glances, those hugs, the spontaneous smiles that would otherwise escape. A good photographer knows how to use light, enhance the location, and move without disturbing the ceremony, so every image looks natural yet meticulously curated. And when you look back at the photos in ten or twenty years, you'll thank yourself for having invested in professionalism. A civil wedding in Turin can be simple and intimate or spectacular and scenic, it depends on what you dream of. The important thing is to plan everything in advance, choose the right location, coordinate other details like flowers, makeup, and accessibility for guests, and above all, ensure that every moment is captured by expert hands. In the end, it's the most important day of your life, and every detail, from the choice of the hall to the light in the photos, will contribute to making it truly unforgettable. A little trick I want to share. If you choose a stately venue, keep an eye on the natural light. Some halls become truly spectacular in the late afternoon, and this makes a huge difference for photos. And speaking of photos, this is no laughing matter. A professional photographer by your side is essential. I'm not just talking about beautiful shots, but about someone who knows how to tell the emotions of the day, capture those glances, those hugs, the spontaneous smiles that would otherwise escape. A good photographer knows how to use light, enhance the location, and move without disturbing the ceremony, so every image looks natural yet meticulously curated. And when you look back at the photos in ten or twenty years, you'll thank yourself for having invested in professionalism. A civil wedding in Turin can be simple and intimate or spectacular and scenic, it depends on what you dream of. The important thing is to plan everything in advance, choose the right location, coordinate other details like flowers, makeup, and accessibility for guests, and above all, ensure that every moment is captured by expert hands. In the end, it's the most important day of your life, and every detail, from the choice of the hall to the light in the photos, will contribute to making it truly unforgettable. We offer professional photography services for civil weddings in the Municipality, ceremonies, and events in Turin and the main provinces of Piedmont, including Alessandria, Asti, Biella, Cuneo, Novara, Verbania, and Vercelli. We operate with method and continuity within municipal venues and institutional spaces, adapting our intervention to the rules, timings, and characteristics of the structure hosting the celebration. We carefully manage both essential civil ceremonies and more complex contexts, ensuring a discreet and orderly presence, in line with the official conduct of the act. We guarantee coverage throughout the territory and a photographic service built on real organizational needs, with particular attention to the clarity of the narrative and the quality of the image. The objective is to document the civil wedding in a precise, sober, and professional manner, enhancing every significant moment without interfering with the ceremony."
