    "excerptEn": "Photography for the MICE Sector: Visual Storytelling for Corporate Events in Piedmont and Aosta Valley In today’s fast-paced communication landscape, imagery is no longer just an accessory; it is a strategic asset. For event agencies and marketing departments, documenting a meeting, a grand opening,",
    "content": "Photography for the MICE Sector: Visual Storytelling for Corporate Events in Piedmont and Aosta Valley In today’s fast-paced communication landscape, imagery is no longer just an accessory it is a strategic asset. For event agencies and marketing departments, documenting a meeting, a grand opening, or an international convention means transforming a fleeting moment into a permanent, high-profile digital asset for editorial and promotional use. Managing the visual documentation of complex events requires a technical approach that goes far beyond traditional photography. My service is built on five core pillars: Institutional Reportage & Grand Openings: Discreet storytelling of ribbon-cutting ceremonies and official protocols, capturing both the atmosphere and high-level portraits without disrupting the proceedings. Workshops & Team Building: Dynamic photography that captures energy, human interaction, and collaboration in both indoor and outdoor settings. Gala Dinners & Award Ceremonies: Expert management of artificial lighting in elegant venues, highlighting lighting design, table settings (mise en place), and the emotional highlights of the awards. Instant Content for Social Media: Real-time delivery of optimized files during the event, enabling marketing teams to provide live coverage on LinkedIn, Instagram, and press outlets. Brand Identity Compliance: Strict adherence to your corporate Brand Manual, ensuring visual and color consistency that aligns with your company values throughout the event. Premier Locations: A Stage Between Innovation and Tradition I operate across the most prestigious areas of Northwest Italy, adapting my photographic technique to the unique characteristics of each venue: Turin: Where Heritage Meets Innovation From the regal atmosphere of the Sabaude Residences (Venaria Reale, Royal Palace) to the cutting-edge tech hubs of OGR or the Lingotto. Turin demands a versatility that bridges historical prestige with post-industrial modernity. The Heart of Piedmont: Business, Textiles, and Logistics Langhe, Roero, and Monferrato (Alba, Asti, Cuneo): Luxury incentive photography and enogastronomic meetings in historic castles and wine estates. Biella and Novara: Documenting workshops in the textile excellence sector, pharmaceuticals, and industrial archaeology spaces. Alessandria and Vercelli: Visual support for technical congresses and trade fairs dedicated to logistics and advanced agritech. Lake Maggiore (Stresa, Baveno): The perfect stage for international conventions and product launches, blending scenic elegance with business efficiency. Aosta Valley: High-Altitude Exclusivity Courmayeur and Cervinia: Technical management of extreme light conditions (snow and glare) for winter product launches and high-adrenaline outdoor activities. Aosta and Saint-Vincent: Historic venues for medical-scientific congresses and institutional summits. Fort Bard: Epic narration for gala evenings and conference exhibitions in a unique, monumental setting. Why Choose a Local Photographic Partner? Collaborating with a professional rooted in the territory guarantees logistical reliability and deep knowledge of the best locations. From a private briefing in Turin to an international conference facing Mont Blanc, my goal remains the same: to deliver images that certify your professionalism. Enrico Scarsi professional photographer in Turin Our studio is located at Via Oropa 54B, Vanchiglietta / Vanchiglia district Close to Corso Belgio and Corso Casale +39 011 8998291 +39 348 9229300 enrico.scarsi@gmail.c om VAT 05529370016 This website does not use any type of cookies, including technical cookies or profiling cookies. Browsing takes place without the collection or tracking of users’ personal data.",
    "contentEn": "Photography for the MICE Sector: Visual Storytelling for Corporate Events in Piedmont and Aosta Valley In today’s fast-paced communication landscape, imagery is no longer just an accessory; it is a strategic asset. For event agencies and marketing departments, documenting a meeting, a grand opening, or an international convention means transforming a fleeting moment into a permanent, high-profile digital asset for editorial and promotional use. Managing the visual documentation of complex events requires a technical approach that goes far beyond traditional photography. My service is built on five core pillars: Institutional Reportage & Grand Openings: Discreet storytelling of ribbon-cutting ceremonies and official protocols, capturing both the atmosphere and high-level portraits without disrupting the proceedings. Workshops & Team Building: Dynamic photography that captures energy, human interaction, and collaboration in both indoor and outdoor settings. Gala Dinners & Award Ceremonies: Expert management of artificial lighting in elegant venues, highlighting lighting design, table settings (mise en place), and the emotional highlights of the awards. Instant Content for Social Media: Real-time delivery of optimized files during the event, enabling marketing teams to provide live coverage on LinkedIn, Instagram, and press outlets. Brand Identity Compliance: Strict adherence to your corporate Brand Manual, ensuring visual and color consistency that aligns with your company values throughout the event. Premier Locations: A Stage Between Innovation and Tradition I operate across the most prestigious areas of Northwest Italy, adapting my photographic technique to the unique characteristics of each venue: Turin: Where Heritage Meets Innovation From the regal atmosphere of the Sabaude Residences (Venaria Reale, Royal Palace) to the cutting-edge tech hubs of OGR or the Lingotto. Turin demands a versatility that bridges historical prestige with post-industrial modernity. The Heart of Piedmont: Business, Textiles, and Logistics Langhe, Roero, and Monferrato (Alba, Asti, Cuneo): Luxury incentive photography and enogastronomic meetings in historic castles and wine estates. Biella and Novara: Documenting workshops in the textile excellence sector, pharmaceuticals, and industrial archaeology spaces. Alessandria and Vercelli: Visual support for technical congresses and trade fairs dedicated to logistics and advanced agritech. Lake Maggiore (Stresa, Baveno): The perfect stage for international conventions and product launches, blending scenic elegance with business efficiency. Aosta Valley: High-Altitude Exclusivity Courmayeur and Cervinia: Technical management of extreme light conditions (snow and glare) for winter product launches and high-adrenaline outdoor activities. Aosta and Saint-Vincent: Historic venues for medical-scientific congresses and institutional summits. Fort Bard: Epic narration for gala evenings and conference exhibitions in a unique, monumental setting. Why Choose a Local Photographic Partner? Collaborating with a professional rooted in the territory guarantees logistical reliability and deep knowledge of the best locations. From a private briefing in Turin to an international conference facing Mont Blanc, my goal remains the same: to deliver images that certify your professionalism. Enrico Scarsi professional photographer in Turin Our studio is located at Via Oropa 54B, Vanchiglietta / Vanchiglia district Close to Corso Belgio and Corso Casale +39 011 8998291 +39 348 9229300 enrico.scarsi@gmail.com VAT 05529370016 This website does not use any type of cookies, including technical cookies or profiling cookies. Browsing takes place without the collection or tracking of users’ personal data."
